---
description: Chart widget — presets, chart types, series configuration
globs: dashboards/**/*.yaml
alwaysApply: false
---

<rule>
<meta>
  This rule covers the `chart` widget for A7S Skipper dashboards: presets, series types, tooltips, multi-track panels, drill-down, ECharts passthrough, and data interpolation.
  Activate when creating or editing chart widgets in dashboard YAML files.
</meta>

<concepts>
  <rendering_engine>ECharts (via echarts-for-react)</rendering_engine>
  <design_system>
    Use canonical chart palettes: `default`, `ocean`, `sunset`.
    Prefer named design-system colors over custom hex.
    Semantic colors (success/warning/error) are for status, not chart decoration.
    If MCP available, inspect `skipper://design-system` and `skipper://design-system/palettes`.
  </design_system>
</concepts>

<schema>
  <chart_widget>
    ```yaml
    - id: my_chart
      type: chart
      col_span: 12
      datasource: web5_costs               # Key, projection name, or inline { sql }
      title: "Web5 Costs"                   # Optional. Widget header title
      chart_title: "Revenue trend"          # Optional. Inside ECharts canvas
      preset: trend                         # Optional. Preset layout
      chart_type: bar                       # Optional. line | bar | combo
      sort: value_desc                      # Optional. X-axis sort
      drill_down: true                      # Optional. Boolean or object
      y_inverse: false                      # Optional. Flip Y-axis
      legend_position: bottom               # Optional. bottom | left | right
      reference_lines: []                   # Optional. Marker lines
      series: []                            # Optional. Series config
      tracks: []                            # Optional. Multi-track panels
      tooltip: {}                           # Optional. Tooltip config
      legend: {}                            # Optional. Legend template
      echarts_options: {}                   # Optional. Raw ECharts overrides
    ```
  </chart_widget>

  <series_config>
    ```yaml
    series:
      - metric: costs                       # Required. Column name
        type: line                          # Optional. line | bar | scatter
        label: "Costs"                      # Optional. Legend label
        color: warning                      # Optional. Named or hex
        format: currency                    # Optional. currency | percent | number
        y_axis: left                        # Optional. left | right (dual axis)
        line_width: 3                       # Optional. Line thickness px
        color_by_value:                     # Optional. Color by sign
          positive: success
          negative: destructive
        band:                               # Optional. CI band
          lower: ci_lower
          upper: ci_upper
          label: "CI band"
        symbol: circle                      # Optional. Scatter marker shape
        symbol_size: 8                      # Optional. Fixed px, or:
        symbol_size:                        #   Dynamic from data column
          column: weight
          min: 6
          max: 20
    ```
  </series_config>
</schema>

<options>
  <presets>
    | Preset | Best for | Default behavior |
    |---|---|---|
    | `trend` | Time series | Line chart, date x-axis, auto-detects time column |
    | `comparison` | Year-over-year | Groups by year/period, overlays for comparison |
    | `breakdown` | Category splits | Stacked/grouped bars by category |
    | `loss_analysis` | Profit/loss | Horizontal bar, negative values go left |
    | `cohort` | Cohort curves | Multi-line, one per cohort group |
    | `multi_track` | Stacked panels | Each series → separate panel, shared X-axis |
  </presets>

  <chart_types>
    | Type | Description |
    |---|---|
    | `line` | Line chart |
    | `bar` | Bar chart (vertical) |
    | `combo` | Mixed bar + line on same axes |
  </chart_types>

  <sort_modes>
    | Value | Description |
    |---|---|
    | `value_desc` | By metric value, largest first |
    | `value_asc` | By metric value, smallest first |
    | `category_asc` | By category name ascending (default) |
    | `category_desc` | By category name descending |
    | `none` | Preserve data source order |

    For grouped charts, `value_desc`/`value_asc` sorts by sum across all groups.
  </sort_modes>

  <named_colors>
    `primary`, `secondary`, `warning`, `neutral`, `destructive`, `success`, `danger`
    Plus hex values: `"#3b82f6"`
    Prefer palette colors for multi-series; use hex only when named tokens insufficient.
  </named_colors>

  <format_priority>
    Resolution order — applies to tooltip, y-axis, and bar labels, including YoY / drill-down charts:

    1. `series[].format` (explicit, per-metric — highest priority)
    2. `tooltip.format_overrides[metric]`
    3. `tooltip.value_format` (tooltip-wide default)
    4. Auto-detection from column name + value range

    Auto-detection heuristic (`detectFormat`):
    - Name contains one of: `revenue`, `cost`, `price`, `amount`, `value`, `profit`, `income`, `loss` → `currency`
    - Name contains one of: `rate`, `percent`, `pct`, `ratio`, `roi` → `percent`
    - All values in `[-1, 1]` → `percent`
    - Otherwise → `number`

    **Metrics whose names lack these keywords** (e.g. `cpa`, `cpm`, `arpu`, `ltv`, `aov`, `ecpm`) **MUST set `format: currency` explicitly on the series** — otherwise currency/percent symbols will be missing in tooltips, axis labels, and bar labels. Do not rely on `tooltip.value_format` alone; set it at series level for consistency across tooltip, y-axis, and labels.
  </format_priority>

  <data_interpolation>
    Markers in `echarts_options`, `reference_lines`, `chart_title`, `series[].label`, `tracks[].title`:

    | Marker | Resolves to | Example |
    |---|---|---|
    | `$column:name` | Array of all values | `["20 Jan", "21 Jan"]` |
    | `$value:name:agg` | Single aggregated value | `42.5` |
    | `$rows` | Full row array | `[{date:"20 Jan", val:1}]` |

    Aggregations: `first`, `last`, `min`, `max`, `sum`, `avg`.
    Pipe chains: `$value:revenue:sum|round:0|currency`
    Available pipes: `round:N`, `floor`, `ceil`, `abs`, `sign`, `fixed:N`, `currency`, `percent`, `number`
  </data_interpolation>
</options>

<examples>
  <trend_chart>
    ```yaml
    - id: crm-revenue
      type: chart
      datasource: crm_activity_revenue
      preset: trend
      title: "CRM Activity Revenue"
      series:
        - metric: revenue_net
          type: line
        - metric: all_revenue
          type: line
          label: "Total"
          color: neutral
    ```
  </trend_chart>

  <comparison_with_drill_down>
    ```yaml
    - id: revenue-yoy
      type: chart
      datasource: revenue_metrics_yoy
      preset: comparison
      drill_down:
        columns: [year, month, day]         # Coarsest → finest (min 2)
        default: month                      # Initial level
        projections:                        # Per-level re-aggregation for ratios
          month: roi_monthly
          year: roi_yearly
      title: "Revenue metrics YoY"
      series:
        - metric: costs
          type: bar
          y_axis: left
        - metric: annual_revenue
          type: line
          color: warning
          y_axis: right
    ```
  </comparison_with_drill_down>

  <loss_analysis>
    ```yaml
    - id: revenue-losses
      type: chart
      datasource: revenue_losses_by_language
      preset: loss_analysis
      title: "Revenue Losses by Language"
      series:
        - metric: profit
    ```
  </loss_analysis>

  <multi_track_explicit>
    ```yaml
    - id: margin-spend
      type: chart
      col_span: 12
      row_span: 2
      datasource: margin_spend_data
      title: "Margin and spend by day"
      tracks:
        - title: "Total margin"
          height_ratio: 1
          series:
            - metric: margin
              type: bar
              color_by_value: { positive: success, negative: destructive }
        - title: "Marketing Costs"
          height_ratio: 1
          series:
            - metric: marketing_costs
              type: line
              color: primary
    ```
  </multi_track_explicit>

  <multi_track_preset>
    Each `series` auto-becomes a track; `label` becomes track title:
    ```yaml
    - id: margin-spend-easy
      type: chart
      col_span: 12
      row_span: 2
      datasource: margin_spend_data
      preset: multi_track
      title: "Margin and spend by day"
      series:
        - metric: margin
          type: bar
          label: "Total margin"
          color_by_value: { positive: success, negative: destructive }
        - metric: marketing_costs
          type: line
          label: "Marketing Costs"
          color: primary
    ```
  </multi_track_preset>

  <scatter_dynamic_size>
    ```yaml
    series:
      - metric: srm_flag
        type: scatter
        label: "SRM markers"
        symbol: circle
        symbol_size:
          column: srm_weight
          min: 8
          max: 16
        color: "#C084FC"
    ```
  </scatter_dynamic_size>

  <confidence_band>
    ```yaml
    series:
      - metric: test
        type: line
        color: "#FF00FF"
        band:
          lower: ci_lower
          upper: ci_upper
          label: "test – uplift CI"
    ```
  </confidence_band>

  <reference_lines>
    ```yaml
    reference_lines:
      - axis: y
        value: 0
        label: "Zero"
        color: "#00E5FF"
        style: solid
      - axis: x
        value: "$value:experiment_start_date:first"
        label: "Experiment start"
        label_position: bottom
        color: "#9CA3AF"
        style: dashed
    ```
  </reference_lines>

  <tooltip_simple>
    ```yaml
    tooltip:
      show_percent: true
      show_change: true
      show_total: true
      value_format: currency
      format_overrides:
        revenue: currency
        rate: percent
    ```
  </tooltip_simple>

  <tooltip_template>
    ```yaml
    tooltip:
      template: |
        <b>{x}</b>
        {#series}
        {marker} {name}: <b>{value|round:0|currency}</b> ({percent|round:1}%)
        {/series}
        <hr/>
        Total: <b>{total|round:0|currency}</b>
    ```

    Tokens: `{x}`, `{#series}...{/series}`, `{marker}`, `{name}`, `{value}`, `{percent}`, `{change}`, `{change_pct}`, `{total}`
    Pipes: `round:N`, `floor`, `ceil`, `abs`, `sign`, `fixed:N`, `currency`, `percent`, `number`
    When `template` is set, simple options are ignored.
  </tooltip_template>

  <legend_template>
    ```yaml
    legend:
      template: "{name}: {last|currency}"
    ```
    Tokens: `{name}`, `{first}`, `{last}`, `{min}`, `{max}`, `{sum}`, `{avg}`. Pipes chainable.
  </legend_template>

  <title_interpolation>
    ```yaml
    - id: revenue-trend
      type: chart
      datasource: daily_revenue
      preset: trend
      chart_title: "Revenue — total $value:revenue:sum|round:0|currency"
      series:
        - metric: revenue
          label: "Revenue ($value:revenue:last|round:0|currency)"
    ```
  </title_interpolation>

  <echarts_raw>
    When `echarts_options` is set WITHOUT `series`/`tracks`/`preset`, the adapter is bypassed:
    ```yaml
    - id: custom-radar
      type: chart
      datasource: radar_data
      echarts_options:
        radar:
          indicator:
            - { name: "Speed", max: 100 }
            - { name: "Power", max: 100 }
        series:
          - type: radar
            data:
              - value: "$column:scores"
    ```
  </echarts_raw>

  <echarts_override>
    When combined with normal config, deep-merges on top:
    ```yaml
    - id: tweaked-chart
      type: chart
      datasource: sales_data
      series:
        - metric: revenue
      echarts_options:
        grid: { left: 120 }
        tooltip: { trigger: item }
    ```
  </echarts_override>
</examples>

<layout>
  <side_by_side_charts>
    Use section `layout: horizontal` for side-by-side charts:

    ```yaml
    sections:
      - id: side-by-side
        title: Side by Side Charts
        layout: horizontal
        columns: 2
        widgets:
          - id: chart-left
            type: chart
            datasource: source_a
            preset: loss_analysis
            series: [{ metric: profit }]
          - id: chart-right
            type: chart
            datasource: source_b
            preset: trend
            series: [{ metric: revenue_net, type: line }]
    ```
  </side_by_side_charts>

  <multi_track_height>
    Use `row_span: 2` or higher for multi-track charts (300px per track, min 400px total).
    Height formula: `row_span * 250` (multi-track) or `row_span * 400` (standard).
  </multi_track_height>
</layout>

<patterns>
  <track_config>
    ```yaml
    tracks:
      - title: string                       # Y-axis label
        height_ratio: number                # Relative height (default 1)
        y_inverse: boolean                  # Invert Y-axis for this track
        soft_min: boolean                   # Soft-clamp Y minimum to 0
        split_area: boolean                 # Alternating horizontal bands
        area_fill: boolean                  # Fill area under lines
        zero_line: boolean                  # Dashed zero reference line
        label_every: number                 # Show labels every N points
        background_fill: string             # Track background color (hex)
        borders:                            # Per-side borders
          enabled: boolean
          top: boolean
          bottom: boolean
          left: boolean
          right: boolean
        axis_line:                          # Y-axis line style
          show: boolean
          color: string
          width: number
          type: solid | dashed | dotted
        series: [...]                       # Required. Series in this panel
    ```
  </track_config>

  <drill_down>
    - `drill_down: true` — auto-detects year/month/day hierarchy
    - `drill_down: { columns: [...], default: ..., projections: {} }` — explicit hierarchy
    - `columns` ordered coarsest → finest (min 2). Active level = `GROUP BY columns.slice(0, indexOf(level) + 1)`
    - `default` is initial aggregation level (defaults to finest)
    - `projections` maps levels to projection keys — use for ratio metrics that can't be summed
    - Supports non-temporal hierarchies: `{ columns: [region, city] }`
    - **Incompatible with `tracks`** (tracks takes priority)
  </drill_down>
</patterns>

<rules>
  <hard_constraints>
    - `datasource` is required — provides data for interpolation
    - `datasource` accepts string key, projection name, or inline `{ sql }`
    - When using `preset`, chart auto-configures axes, legends, tooltips
    - `chart_type` overrides preset default type
    - If no `series`, chart auto-detects numeric columns
    - `tracks` takes priority over `series` if both specified
    - `tracks` incompatible with `drill_down`
    - `title` = widget header; `chart_title` = inside ECharts canvas
    - `band` columns and `symbol_size.column` are excluded from auto-detected metrics
    - Raw echarts mode bypasses all adapter logic; override mode deep-merges (objects merged, arrays replaced)
    - For metrics whose names don't match currency/percent keywords (`cpa`, `cpm`, `arpu`, `ltv`, `aov`, `ecpm`, ...) you MUST set `format: currency` (or the appropriate type) on the series explicitly — auto-detection will fall back to `number` and strip the `$` / `%` symbol
  </hard_constraints>
</rules>

<see_also>
  - `dashboard-datasources` — datasource reference patterns, projections for drill-down
  - `dashboard-yaml-structure` — grid layout, section horizontal for side-by-side charts
  - `dashboard-builder-guide` — chart patterns, conventions
</see_also>
</rule>
